This file states Exercise 4.17. For elements of a monoid, the least subset equal to the union of the unit, those two elements, and the pointwise square is the submonoid they generate. The operator is monotone, so the least-fixed-point construction on the power set applies, and a fixed point is a submonoid containing the two elements. The whole carrier is another fixed point, because each element is the product of the unit with itself. In the multiplicative monoid of the natural numbers, with both generators equal to one, the singleton of one and the whole set are distinct fixed points. The file imports the operator, the packaging of a pre-fixed point as a submonoid, and the membership of the unit, the generators, and the pointwise square.
